185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (Have children sit on a swing, desk chair, or Bilibo chair. Guide them to take a slow, deep breath in as they swing or rotate in one direction, then exhale slowly as they move in the opposite direction. Encourage them to observe their environment, noting colors and sounds. Ask them to describe how their body feels \(e.g., "hands are tight," "feet are light"\). Prompt them to notice if breathing is easier in a particular direction and if they have a preferred direction of movement.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
