239 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (Have children sit or lie in a comfortable position. Ask them to place both hands gently on their belly. Guide them to take slow, deep breaths, focusing on the movement of their belly. Encourage them to feel their belly rise as they inhale and fall as they exhale. Use simple language to explain the process, such as "Let's make our tummy big like a balloon when we breathe in, and then let it get small when we breathe out." Continue this for 5-10 breaths or as long as the children remain engaged.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
