462 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 113 0 R
/E (As the child performs this activity, observe their body awareness by noticing if they can easily locate their ears without looking. Pay attention to their bilateral coordination, watching how well they can control movements on both sides of their body. Look for any hesitation or difficulty when the child reaches across their body, which indicates their ability to cross the midline. Observe their fine motor control, looking for smooth, controlled movements as they trace their ear. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
